1
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:09,160
Some road signs show a gradient.

2
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:15,380
A gradient of 1 in 8 means the road rises 1 metre for every 8 metres across.

3
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:17,250
Lines have gradients too.

4
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:22,510
Which is steeper: y equals 2 x plus 1, or y equals 3 x minus 4?

5
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:24,000
Which line is steeper?

6
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:27,210
Pause the video and choose.

7
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:29,580
y equals 3 x minus 4 is steeper.

8
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:31,940
It goes up 3 for every 1 across.

9
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,520
y equals 2 x plus 1 only goes up 2.

10
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:38,690
The number in front of x tells you the steepness.

11
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:43,360
Remember: y equals 2 x plus 1 passes through 0, 1 and 1, 3.

12
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:48,500
And y equals 3 x minus 4 crosses the y axis at negative 4.

13
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:51,260
In y equals m x plus c, m is the gradient.

14
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:54,210
It is how much y goes up when x goes up by 1.

15
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:58,430
c is the y intercept, where the line crosses the y axis.

16
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,150
Your turn.

17
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,490
What is the intercept of y equals 5 x minus 2?

18
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:05,850
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,760
The intercept is negative 2.

20
00:01:07,810 --> 00:01:12,070
To find a gradient from a graph, choose two points on the line.

21
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:16,170
The gradient is the change in y, divided by the change in x.

22
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:17,680
Rise over run.

23
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:22,520
From A at 1, 3, to B at 4, 9: the rise is 6, and the run is 3.

24
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:24,080
6 divided by 3 is 2.

25
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:28,690
The line crosses at 1, so it is y equals 2 x plus 1.

26
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:30,000
Here is the method.

27
00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:35,190
Step 1: read the y intercept, c, where the line crosses the y axis.

28
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:37,430
Step 2: choose two clear points.

29
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,660
The gradient m is rise over run.

30
00:01:39,710 --> 00:01:42,940
It is negative if the line slopes down.

31
00:01:42,990 --> 00:01:45,930
Step 3: write y equals m x plus c.

32
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:49,730
Step 4: check with another point on the line.

33
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:53,070
A line goes through 0, negative 3, and 2, 5.

34
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:57,870
It crosses the y axis at negative 3, so c is negative 3.

35
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:01,360
The rise is 5 minus negative 3, which is 8.

36
00:02:01,410 --> 00:02:02,410
The run is 2.

37
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:04,030
8 divided by 2 is 4.

38
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,530
So y equals 4 x minus 3.

39
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:07,280
Your turn.

40
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:11,450
What is the gradient of the line through 0, 1, and 2, 7?

41
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:14,490
Pause and work it out.

42
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:17,320
The rise is 7 minus 1, which is 6.

43
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:18,400
The run is 2.

44
00:02:18,450 --> 00:02:20,620
6 divided by 2 is 3.

45
00:02:20,670 --> 00:02:23,320
A line goes through 0, 6 and 3, 0.

46
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:23,880
c is 6.

47
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:27,140
The line goes down 6 as it goes across 3.

48
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:30,160
Negative 6 divided by 3 is negative 2.

49
00:02:30,210 --> 00:02:33,250
So y equals negative 2 x plus 6.

50
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:36,120
Parallel lines have the same gradient.

51
00:02:36,170 --> 00:02:42,600
A line parallel to y equals 5 x minus 1, through 0, 4, has gradient 5 and intercept 4.

52
00:02:42,650 --> 00:02:45,110
It is y equals 5 x plus 4.

53
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:48,730
Finn finds the gradient through 2, 1 and 6, 3.

54
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:51,480
Which line goes wrong first?

55
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:52,540
Line 2 is wrong.

56
00:02:52,590 --> 00:02:54,600
He divided the run by the rise.

57
00:02:54,650 --> 00:02:59,060
The gradient is the change in y divided by the change in x.

58
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:01,760
2 divided by 4 is a half.

59
00:03:01,810 --> 00:03:05,980
Building rules limit how steep a wheelchair ramp can be.

60
00:03:06,030 --> 00:03:08,980
A common limit is a gradient of 1 in 12.

61
00:03:09,030 --> 00:03:12,620
That means 1 unit up for every 12 across.

62
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:19,670
So to rise 60 centimetres, a ramp needs to be about 7.2 metres long across the ground.

63
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:20,950
One last question.

64
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,850
Which line is parallel to y equals negative 2 x plus 1?

65
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:28,170
Pause the video and choose.

66
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:31,890
Parallel lines have the same gradient, negative 2.

67
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:35,780
So y equals negative 2 x minus 5 is parallel.

68
00:03:35,830 --> 00:03:41,440
To remember: in y equals m x plus c, m is the gradient and c is the y intercept.

69
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:43,290
Gradient is rise over run.

70
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,120
A negative gradient slopes down.

71
00:03:46,170 --> 00:03:49,230
Parallel lines have the same gradient.

72
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:53,060
Rearrange to y equals something, to read m and c.

73
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:58,470
Great work! Now practise lesson 11.3 on Camday.
